// 6. protected

// protected is similar to private, but it becomes important when we learn inheritance.

// For now, remember:

// Access	Same Class	Outside Class	Child/Derived Class
// public	✅	✅	✅
// private	✅	❌	❌
// protected	✅	❌	✅

// Example:

// class Vehicle {
// protected:
//     int speed;
// };

// Outside code cannot do:

// Vehicle v;


// // v.speed = 100; ❌

// But when another class inherits from Vehicle, it can access speed.

// class Car : public Vehicle {
// public:
//     void setSpeed() {
//         speed = 100; // ✅ Allowed
//     }
// };

// You don't need to deeply focus on protected yet. It will make much more sense when you start inheritance.

